     If Spork hasn't implemented deafness yet then you
probably managed to toggle the `sound' option off.  It's
used for two not very compatible things:  controlling
whether your character can hear (so the program toggles
it off if you faint from hunger, then back on again when
you regain consciousness) and also whether the player
wants to suppress atmospheric messages like fountains
splashing (so you can toggle this manually via the 'O'
command).  Unfortunately, doing the latter interferes
with verbalized messages in addition to background noises;
also for the former, the game overrides the user's option
setting once hearing has returned.  NetHack's post-3.4.3
code has split involuntary deafness off from voluntary
hushing to fix this.


